#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_conversation
msgid ""
"\n"
"Conversations\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"A ``conversation.conversation`` is one recorded call, meeting or field visit: who\n"
"is responsible, the customer, the people known to take part, and its recordings\n"
"as a media timeline. It is a business record over the import cycle, not a\n"
"pipeline of its own:\n"
"\n"
"- **Transcription** is ``speech``'s: each recording is a segment, transcribed by\n"
"  whichever engine the company's ``gateway_ml`` policy allows for\n"
"  ``speech.transcription.<kind>`` (sensitive), or on the server by\n"
"  ``speech_local``. Domain vocabulary (``speech.vocabulary``, extended here with\n"
"  crops and active ingredients) travels as key terms. How long the audio is kept\n"
"  is ``conversation.retention.policy``; the transcript outlives it.\n"
"- **Voices** are ``speech.speaker`` rows, named after the attendees, by the\n"
"  analyst's guesses, by elimination, by employee name, or by\n"
"  ``speech_voiceprint`` when it is installed.\n"
"- **Analysis** is ``speech_analysis``'s, under the ``conversation`` schema, which\n"
"  inherits ``speech_analysis`` and adds the outcome, recommendations and proposed\n"
"  actions. The analyst reads a context header -- the company's\n"
"  ``analysis_context``, the known people, the vocabulary, the tool catalog --\n"
"  before the transcript, under the purpose ``speech.analysis.conversation``.\n"
"- **Proposed actions** are ``ai.tool.call`` rows of the catalog's tools\n"
"  (``ir.actions.server`` flagged ``conversation_enabled``). Each tool names the\n"
"  approval category that decides it -- the person in charge, a leader, a\n"
"  manager -- and runs, once approved, as the person it was proposed for. The\n"
"  generic create and update tools write only what ``ai.tool.model.access``\n"
"  allows.\n"
"\n"
"``conversation_meeting`` adds the meeting room and live coaching,\n"
"``conversation_mobile`` the company phones, and ``conversation_sale``,\n"
"``_purchase``, ``_mrp`` and ``_account`` their own tools.\n"
msgstr ""

